    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 all 14 tests pass, including the two new `Cp07Tests`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the registration-date feature for `POST /api/owners` so that a supplied date is preserved and an omitted one defaults to the server's current date, returned as ISO `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added an optional `registrationDate` field (`type: string, format: date`) to the `OwnerFields` schema. Because `Owner` extends `OwnerFields`, this makes it both an input on create and an output on read; the generated DTOs (`OwnerFieldsDto`/`OwnerDto`) get a `java.time.LocalDate` field that Jackson serializes as `YYYY-MM-DD`.\n\n2. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `LocalDate registrationDate` field (mapped to column `registration_date`) with getter/setter. MapStruct maps it by name automatically in both directions.\n\n3. **DB schemas** \u2014 added a `registration_date DATE` column to the owners table in all four schema files (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql). The test suite runs under the **hsqldb** profile with `ddl-auto=none`, so that schema had to carry the column.\n\n4. **`DefaultOwnerRegistrationDate.java`** \u2014 a new OfficeFloor function that mutates the built `Owner` in place, setting `registrationDate` to `LocalDate.now()` only when the request omitted it.\n\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 wired the new step into the create pipeline between `build` and `save`, under the same `transaction` governance.\n\nA supplied date flows through `BuildOwner` untouched; an absent one is defaulted; either way `RespondWithOwner` (via `GET /api/owners/{id}`) returns it in ISO form.",
